if that also fails to the SVD estimates (\code{method = "svd"} with \code{adjust = "dt"}). Their forecasts are not those of the Poisson Lee-Carter model;
wider age groups (\code{\link[=mt_regroup]{mt_regroup()}}) or pooling (\code{\link[=li_lee]{li_lee()}}) avoid them.

Draws describe the expected rates. Predictive draws
(\code{mt_forecast(predictive = TRUE)}) add Poisson variation of the deaths
given the rates and the exposures, the observation model of the Poisson
Lee-Carter model (Brouhns, Denuit and Vermunt 2002); no other observation
noise is added. If intervals are too narrow on real data, that is a
